DECISIONS 214, TYPES.md §1, GRAMMAR.md §2.6, §8.2: an empty interpolation in an annotation's template (a pairs element, @files) breaks its declaration and is not judged further: no E1119 "expected a template string" beside the E1112. A comment inside an interpolation keeps its expression, so that template stays judged and sound (non-regression line).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

record R {
  g: [P] @json(pairs: ["k{i}", "{}v{i}"])
  h: [P] @json(pairs: ["k{i /* c */}", "v{i}"])
}

@files("{}.json")
let y = 2
-- findings.txt --
error[E1112]  a/a.canon:4:33
  invalid interpolation: {} is empty

error[E1112]  a/a.canon:5:29
  invalid interpolation: a comment inside it

error[E1112]  a/a.canon:8:9
  invalid interpolation: {} is empty

3 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
